 "function": "cloudgen.texture.regime_texture",
 "doc": "Plans in call order: 0-1 the generic fBm (seed+3, directions 0.75 p + 0.25 back), 2-3 the street fBm (seed+5, 0.1 p + 0.9 back), then a (worley3, cell_edges) pair for each USED cell diameter (seed + int(d_km), directions 0.85 p + 0.15 back); params.cells_used_km lists them, the fBm ladder is octave_ladder(fine_frequency, fmax) (the plans hold its result). The cells are accumulated in float32 and standardized over the WHOLE array (a global mean and std: the case is one array). fmax = 20 on a 6371 km body: even the 120 km cells (f = 53) are finer than the map resolves, none is used, `if used` is skipped (the texture is the generic fBm blended with the street fBm by the street weight only; the closed and open weights are ignored) and there are only 4 plans (no worley3). Measured worst difference 7.1e-5 against float64, 5.9e-5 under a one-ulp nudge: atol 8e-4, rtol 1e-5 (10x). Outputs besides `texture` are the intermediates, there to localize a mismatch: generic_std and street_std (the standardized fBm fields), and, when a cell diameter is used, closed_sum and open_sum (the float32 weighted sums of the cell ramps, before standardization) and closed_std / open_std (their standardizations); each has its own measured tolerance, see TEX_INTER in the case module. params.constants holds the mixes, ramps and seed offsets written in the code, and params.cells_per_radian the f = radius_km / d_km compared with fmax for each diameter (`f > fmax` skips, a tie f == fmax is USED; f is computed by a division).",
